    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "✨ CAPSTONE: Apex Bow. The last thing the old world ever built right. It doesn't miss. Neither do you. It was never going to drop from a monster. It was always going to be GIVEN — to someone who'd earned the shape of it."
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "📓 Codex: The System granted you the Apex Bow — a finished The Apex Predator build recognized."
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "Godhood demands its price, and the price is not hidden: Once per fight — it's set before the first blow. You can't re-choose mid-fight. If it reaches you, you're just a person with a bow. The terms only matter until contact."
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "🕯️ Theo is dead — and the dead hold no treaties. Every link Haven has shakes."
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "Ashford watches to see if Haven holds without its dead — and presses the tribute down to 1,266 kcal/week while the chair is empty. They'll test the link. Count on it. (Trust -8.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "With Haven grieving again, Thornfield installs their own speaker at the table — and reaches for the grief card once more. The table has heard it before: the grief card is spent. Tribute stays at 11,250 kcal/week. The link holds — it was never with one person. (Trust -8.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 95,
      "line": "The Hungry Road watches to see if Haven holds without its dead — and presses the tribute down to 3,000 kcal/week while the chair is empty. They'll test the link. Count on it. (Trust -8.)"
    },
    {
